+# Pre-ship review — USDC Payouts dApp (Base)
+
+Reviewed at `a03517f` (clean tree). Scope: `packages/nextjs` frontend + configuration.
+Verification done: read all frontend source, ran `yarn check-types` (passes), `yarn lint`
+(0 errors, 100 prettier warnings), `yarn next build` (**fails**), and `next dev` against
+`/payouts` (**HTTP 500**).
+
+No code was changed. Build artifacts created during review were removed.
+
+**Verdict: do not ship.** The app does not currently render at all — see B1. There are
+also two fund-safety issues (B2, B3) and a feed that can never load (B4).
+
+---
+
+## Ship-blocking
+
+### B1 — The app returns HTTP 500 on every route; `next build` fails
+
+**File:** `packages/nextjs/components/ScaffoldEthAppWithProviders.tsx:50` (and
+`packages/nextjs/package.json:22`, `@rainbow-me/rainbowkit` 2.2.9)
+
+`next build` aborts during prerender and `next dev` serves a 500 for `/payouts`:
+
+```
+TypeError: localStorage.getItem is not a function
+    at c3 (.next/server/chunks/ssr/...)   // rainbowkit getRecentWalletIds
+    at c4 (...)                           // useWalletConnectors
+    at dm (...)                           // RainbowKitProvider
+Export encountered an error on /_not-found/page, exiting the build.
+```
+
+Root cause: RainbowKit's recent-wallet helper guards with `typeof localStorage !== "undefined"`:
+
+```js
+function getRecentWalletIds() {
+  return typeof localStorage !== "undefined" ? parse(localStorage.getItem("rk-recent")) : [];
+}
+```
+
+Next 16 runs its render/build workers with Node's Web Storage flag enabled (note the
+`--localstorage-file was provided without a valid path` warning), so on the server
+`localStorage` **exists** but is not a functioning Storage object. The `typeof` guard
+passes and `.getItem` blows up inside `RainbowKitProvider`'s render — which is in the
+root provider tree, so it takes down every page.
+
+I reproduced this on Node 22.23.1 and Node 25.9.0, with and without the harness's
+`NODE_OPTIONS`. It is not specific to `/payouts`.
+
+**Fix:** don't render the RainbowKit subtree during SSR. `ScaffoldEthAppWithProviders`
+already tracks `mounted`; gate on it instead of only using it to pick a theme:
+
+```tsx
+const [mounted, setMounted] = useState(false);
+useEffect(() => setMounted(true), []);
+
+return (
+  <WagmiProvider config={wagmiConfig}>
+    <QueryClientProvider client={queryClient}>
+      {mounted ? (
+        <RainbowKitProvider avatar={BlockieAvatar} theme={isDarkMode ? darkTheme() : lightTheme()}>
+          <ProgressBar height="3px" color="#2299dd" />
+          <ScaffoldEthApp>{children}</ScaffoldEthApp>
+        </RainbowKitProvider>
+      ) : null}
+    </QueryClientProvider>
+  </WagmiProvider>
+);
+```
+
+Then re-run `yarn next build` and confirm all 8 pages prerender. If you prefer not to
+lose SSR of page content, the alternative is bumping `@rainbow-me/rainbowkit` to a
+release whose guard is `typeof window !== "undefined"`, or pinning the Next build
+workers off Web Storage — but the `mounted` gate is the change I'd make this week.
+
+---
+
+### B2 — Payout transactions are not pinned to Base; a wrong-chain wallet sends real funds to the wrong contract
+
+**File:** `packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx:6,21,36–62`
+
+The page uses raw wagmi `useWriteContract` with hardcoded Base addresses pulled from
+`deployedContracts[8453]`, and passes no `chainId`:
+
+```ts
+const { writeContractAsync, isPending } = useWriteContract();
+await writeContractAsync({ address: USDC.address, abi: USDC.abi, functionName: "approve", ... });
+```
+
+wagmi sends on whatever chain the wallet is currently on. A user connected to Ethereum
+mainnet, Optimism, Arbitrum, etc. gets a transaction to `0x8335...2913` /
+`0x7c3f...b6F2` **on that chain**, which are not USDC and not Payouts there. There is no
+"wrong network" guard and no simulation, so the only thing between the user and a
+bad/failed transaction is their wallet's own warnings.
+
+The project's own `useScaffoldWriteContract` already handles all of this — it checks
+`accountChain.id !== selectedNetwork.id`, simulates before sending, and surfaces errors
+via `useTransactor`. AGENTS.md mandates it.
+
+**Fix:** replace the raw hook with two scaffold hooks and drop the manual `address`/`abi`:
+
+```ts
+const { writeContractAsync: writeUsdc, isMining: isApproving } = useScaffoldWriteContract({
+  contractName: "USDC",
+});
+const { writeContractAsync: writePayouts, isMining: isPaying } = useScaffoldWriteContract({
+  contractName: "Payouts",
+});
+
+await writeUsdc({ functionName: "approve", args: [payoutsAddress, parseUnits(amount, 6)] });
+await writePayouts({ functionName: "pay", args: [recipient, parseUnits(amount, 6), memo] });
+```
+
+with `payoutsAddress` from `useDeployedContractInfo({ contractName: "Payouts" })` rather
+than the direct `deployedContracts[8453]` import (see S4).
+
+---
+
+### B3 — No recipient or amount validation; invalid input is silently swallowed
+
+**File:** `packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx:55,49–62,78–91`
+
+```ts
+args: [recipient as `0x${string}`, parseUnits(amount || "0", 6), memo],
+```
+
+The `as \`0x${string}\`` cast is a lie — `recipient` is free-form user text. Concretely:
+
+- Empty or malformed recipient → viem throws on encoding, caught by `catch (e) { console.error(e) }`. The user clicks "Send Payout" and **nothing visible happens**.
+- `type="number"` accepts `-5` and `1e3`. `parseUnits("-5", 6)` produces a negative value that fails uint256 encoding — again swallowed silently.
+- Empty amount falls back to `parseUnits("0", 6)`, which the contract reverts on (`Payouts: zero amount`) after the user has already signed.
+- No check against `usdcBalance`, so over-balance payouts fail at the wallet/revert stage.
+
+For a money-moving flow shipping to real users, a button that does nothing and logs to a
+console nobody opens is not acceptable.
+
+**Fix:** validate before enabling the buttons, and show why they're disabled:
+
+```ts
+import { isAddress } from "viem";
+
+const parsedAmount = (() => {
+  try { return amount ? parseUnits(amount, 6) : 0n; } catch { return null; }
+})();
+
+const recipientValid = isAddress(recipient);
+const amountValid = parsedAmount !== null && parsedAmount > 0n
+  && (usdcBalance === undefined || parsedAmount <= usdcBalance);
+const canPay = recipientValid && amountValid && !isPaying;
+```
+
+and use `AddressInput` from `@scaffold-ui/components` for the recipient field, which does
+validation and ENS resolution for free (AGENTS.md § UI Components).
+
