+
+### B4 — The payouts feed scans 33.7M Base blocks and will never load
+
+**File:** `packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx:29–34`
+
+```ts
+useScaffoldEventHistory({ contractName: "Payouts", eventName: "Paid", fromBlock: 0n, watch: true });
+```
+
+`useScaffoldEventHistory` defaults `fromBlock` to the contract's `deployedOnBlock`
+(`33712450`, present in `deployedContracts.ts:46`) — the explicit `0n` throws that away.
+The hook pages in `blocksBatchSize` chunks of 500, so this is roughly **67,000 sequential
+`eth_getLogs` calls** before the first payout ever renders. On Base's public RPC (the
+primary transport — see S1) it will rate-limit long before that, and `watch: true` never
+activates because polling only starts once `hasNextPage` is false. Users see
+"No payouts yet." indefinitely.
+
+**Fix:** delete the `fromBlock: 0n` line so the hook uses `deployedOnBlock`. That is still
+~2,500 requests and growing — acceptable for launch week, but the hook is explicitly
+`@deprecated` for non-local chains ("It can overload RPC endpoints (especially on L2s)").
+Before real traffic, move the feed to an indexer (`.agents/skills/ponder/SKILL.md` or
+`subgraph`), or at minimum add `blocksBatchSize: 10_000` with a dedicated Alchemy
+endpoint that supports it.
+
+---
+
+### B5 — Users get no feedback on any transaction: success, failure, or pending
+
+**File:** `packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx:44–46,59–61`
+
+Both handlers end in `catch (e) { console.error(e); }`. There is no success toast, no
+"transaction mined" confirmation, no error surfaced, and no balance-refresh
+acknowledgement. `handlePay` clears `amount` and `memo` on the optimistic path only, so a
+user who has a tx rejected in their wallet keeps their inputs, while a user whose tx is
+merely *submitted* sees the form clear before it is mined — reading as "done" when it
+isn't.
+
+**Fix:** adopting `useScaffoldWriteContract` (B2) gives you `useTransactor`'s full
+pending/mined/error toasts for free. Keep the `catch` for anything that escapes, but route
+it through the project's helpers per AGENTS.md:
+
+```ts
+} catch (e) {
+  notification.error(getParsedError(e));
+}
+```
+
+and only clear the form inside the `onBlockConfirmation` callback.
+
+---
+
+### B6 — Approve/Pay is a two-button guessing game with no allowance check
+
+**File:** `packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx:99–114`; `packages/nextjs/contracts/deployedContracts.ts:49–134`
+
+The UI shows "Approve" and "Send Payout" side by side with no indication of which is
+needed. The obvious action is "Send Payout" — which, with zero allowance, reverts at the
+wallet with a raw revert string (and, per B5, nothing in the UI). Compounding it:
+
+- The page never reads `allowance`, and **the generated USDC ABI has no `allowance` entry** (only `approve`, `balanceOf`, `decimals`, `symbol`, `transfer`, `transferFrom`, and the `Approval`/`Transfer` events), so it currently *can't*.
+- `handleApprove` approves exactly the current `amount`. Edit the amount after approving and the payout reverts again.
+
+**Fix:** add USDC to `packages/nextjs/contracts/externalContracts.ts` under chain `8453`
+with a full ERC-20 ABI including `allowance` (`deployedContracts.ts` is autogenerated —
+don't hand-edit it), then drive a single button off the allowance:
+
+```ts
+const { data: allowance } = useScaffoldReadContract({
+  contractName: "USDC",
+  functionName: "allowance",
+  args: [connectedAddress, payoutsAddress],
+});
+
+const needsApproval = allowance !== undefined && parsedAmount !== null && allowance < parsedAmount;
+```
+
+Render one primary button labelled "Approve USDC" or "Send Payout" depending on
+`needsApproval`, and re-check allowance after the approve confirms.
+
