+
+## Should-fix
+
+### S1 — Production ships on Scaffold-ETH's shared demo Alchemy key and WalletConnect project ID
+
+**File:** `packages/nextjs/scaffold.config.ts:16,29,40`
+
+`DEFAULT_ALCHEMY_API_KEY = "IZYEU2cWBgnFmgiTAgpWD"` and
+`walletConnectProjectId` default `'3a8170812b534d0ff9d794f19a901d64'` are the public
+SE-2 demo credentials, shared by every scaffold project on the internet. Two consequences:
+
+- `wagmiConfig.tsx:20` deliberately *demotes* the Alchemy transport to last position when the default key is detected, so your primary Base RPC becomes the public `https://mainnet.base.org` — aggressively rate-limited, and the worst possible backing for B4's log queries.
+- A throttled shared WalletConnect project ID means mobile/WalletConnect connections fail intermittently, with no useful error.
+
+`.env.example` lists both vars but leaves them blank, and there's no `.env.local`.
+
+**Fix:** provision your own Alchemy Base key and WalletConnect project ID and set
+`NEXT_PUBLIC_ALCHEMY_API_KEY` / `NEXT_PUBLIC_WALLET_CONNECT_PROJECT_ID` in the Vercel
+project env (all environments) before the deploy. Verify after deploy that the app is not
+falling back to the default-key path.
+
+---
+
+### S2 — `pollingInterval: 30000` makes a 2-second-block L2 feel broken
+
+**File:** `packages/nextjs/scaffold.config.ts:24`
+
+30s is *raised* from the SE-2 default of 4000, on Base, where blocks land every 2s. Balance
+updates, the payouts feed, and `useScaffoldReadContract`'s block-driven invalidation all lag
+up to half a minute — a user who just sent a payout watches a stale balance and an empty
+feed. AGENTS.md explicitly says to *decrease* polling interval for L2 chains.
+
+**Fix:** set `pollingInterval: 4000` (or lower). This raises RPC volume, which is another
+reason to land S1 first.
+
+---
+
+### S3 — Payouts page hardcodes `bg-black text-white`, breaking the theme
+
+**File:** `packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx:65`
+
+`<div className="min-h-screen bg-black text-white">` ignores daisyUI's `light`/`dark`
+themes defined in `styles/globals.css`. In light mode the page is a black slab between a
+white header and footer, and the daisyUI-themed `input input-bordered` / `textarea` fields
+render light-on-light inside it — low-contrast and, for the amount field, close to
+unreadable. The theme switcher in the footer has no effect on this page. AGENTS.md
+§ Styling requires daisyUI semantic classes.
+
+**Fix:** use theme tokens — `<div className="min-h-screen bg-base-200 text-base-content">`
+— and wrap the form in a `card bg-base-100 shadow-xl` like the rest of the app. Also
+replace the hand-rolled `shorten()` (line 13) and the raw `<div className="border
+border-gray-700 ...">` feed rows (line 121) with the `Address` component from
+`@scaffold-ui/components`, which gives ENS names, avatars, and Basescan links.
+
+---
+
+### S4 — Contract data imported directly from `deployedContracts[8453]` instead of via hooks
+
+**File:** `packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx:7,10–11`
+
+```ts
+const PAYOUTS = deployedContracts[8453].Payouts;
+const USDC = deployedContracts[8453].USDC;
+```
+
+This hardcodes the chain ID at module scope, bypasses `useDeployedContractInfo`, and will
+break silently (TypeScript error at best, wrong-chain writes at worst) the moment
+`targetNetworks` changes — e.g. adding Base Sepolia for a staging deploy. AGENTS.md:
+"Always use hooks from `packages/nextjs/hooks/scaffold-eth` for contract interactions."
+
+**Fix:** `const { data: payoutsInfo } = useDeployedContractInfo({ contractName: "Payouts" })`
+and read `payoutsInfo?.address`. Folding in B2 removes the need for the ABI import entirely.
+
+---
+
+### S5 — Event feed uses array-index keys against a reversed, live-updating list
+
+**File:** `packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx:120–121`
+
+```tsx
+{(payouts ?? []).map((payout, i) => (<div key={i} ...>
+```
+
+`useScaffoldEventHistory` reverses the list (newest first) and, with `watch: true`,
+prepends new events. Index keys therefore remap every existing row on each new payout,
+so React reuses DOM nodes across different payouts — stale text, mis-anchored content, and
+broken animations/selection.
+
+**Fix:** key on something stable from the log:
+`key={`${payout.transactionHash}-${payout.logIndex}`}`. While here, the feed also has no
+loading state — it shows "No payouts yet." during the (very long, per B4) initial fetch.
+Destructure `isLoading` from the hook and render a `loading loading-spinner` instead.
+
+---
+
+### S6 — Zero balance and loading balance are indistinguishable
+
+**File:** `packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx:75`
+
+```tsx
+{usdcBalance !== undefined ? formatUnits(usdcBalance, 6) : "0"}
+```
+
+A user whose balance hasn't loaded sees "Your balance: 0 USDC" — reading as "I have no
+money" rather than "still loading". Raw `formatUnits` also prints full 6-decimal precision
+(`1234.500000`).
+
+**Fix:** render a skeleton/spinner while `usdcBalance === undefined`, and format for
+humans: `Number(formatUnits(usdcBalance, 6)).toLocaleString(undefined, { maximumFractionDigits: 2 })`.
+
+---
+
+### S7 — A single `isPending` drives both buttons
+
+**File:** `packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx:100–113`
+
+Both buttons share one `useWriteContract` instance, so approving shows a spinner on "Send
+Payout" too, and vice versa. Neither is disabled for a reason the user can see.
+
+**Fix:** falls out of B2 — two `useScaffoldWriteContract` instances give you independent
+`isMining` flags. Combine with B3's `canPay` for the `disabled` state. Note also that
+daisyUI 5 replaced the `loading` class with `loading loading-spinner` as a child element;
+`btn-primary loading` (line 101) is a no-op on this version, so the buttons currently show
+no spinner at all.
+
+---
+
+### S8 — Production deploy command disables TypeScript errors
+
+**File:** `packages/nextjs/next.config.ts:7–9`; `packages/nextjs/package.json:16`
+
+`ignoreBuildErrors: process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_IGNORE_BUILD_ERROR === "true"`, and
+`vercel:yolo` — the deploy command AGENTS.md documents for this project — sets exactly
+that var to `true`. So the command you ship with is the one that skips type checking.
+Types currently pass (`yarn check-types` is clean), so this costs nothing today and
+guarantees a silent regression later.
+
+**Fix:** deploy with `yarn vercel --prod` (the non-yolo script) for real releases, or drop
+`NEXT_PUBLIC_IGNORE_BUILD_ERROR=true` from `vercel:yolo`. Keep `yarn check-types` in CI —
+`.github/` currently has no workflow enforcing it.
+
+---
+
+### S9 — The app still presents itself as the Scaffold-ETH 2 demo
+
+**Files:** `packages/nextjs/app/layout.tsx:10–13`, `packages/nextjs/app/page.tsx:20–45`,
+`packages/nextjs/components/Header.tsx:95–96`
+
+Shipping to real users with:
+
+- Page title / OG metadata: "Scaffold-ETH 2 App" — "Built with 🏗 Scaffold-ETH 2". Every share link and browser tab says this.
+- Landing page: "Welcome to Scaffold-ETH 2", "Get started by editing `packages/nextjs/app/page.tsx`", "Edit your smart contract `YourContract.sol`" (a contract that doesn't exist in this repo — it's `Payouts.sol`), and "Explore your local transactions".
+- Header logo/text: "Scaffold-ETH / Ethereum dev stack".
+- **The landing page never links to `/payouts`**, the product.
+
+**Fix:** set real metadata in `layout.tsx` (`getMetadata({ title: "USDC Payouts", description: ... })`),
+replace `app/page.tsx` with a short intro plus a primary CTA to `/payouts`, and update the
+header branding. Also confirm `VERCEL_PROJECT_PRODUCTION_URL` is set so
+`getMetadata`'s `baseUrl` (`utils/scaffold-eth/getMetadata.ts:5–7`) doesn't fall back to
+`http://localhost:3000` for OG image URLs.
+
