+
+### S10 — Developer-only routes are exposed in the production nav
+
+**Files:** `packages/nextjs/components/Header.tsx:29–33`, `packages/nextjs/app/blockexplorer/page.tsx`
+
+"Debug Contracts" is a permanent nav item, giving any user a raw write interface to
+`Payouts.pay` and USDC `approve`/`transfer` on mainnet Base, with no guardrails. Worse,
+`/blockexplorer` is still routable (it's reachable directly, and `Footer.tsx:36` links to
+it) and is localhost-only by design — on Base it pops an error toast telling the user
+their "targetNetwork is not localhost", which reads as a broken app.
+
+**Fix:** gate the debug link on `targetNetwork.id === hardhat.id` (the Header already
+computes `isLocalNetwork` at line 67 for the faucet button — reuse it), and either delete
+`app/blockexplorer/` or gate it the same way.
+
